4 5 6
7 8 9
```
(from P1 rows, P4 columns) has rows {1,2,3},{4,5,6},{7,8,9} (all APs with d=1) and columns {1,4,7},{2,5,8},{3,6,9} (all APs with d=3). ✓

## Answer

The number of distinct valid arrangements is $\boxed{288}$.

